{title: You Have Trusted In Me}
{subtitle: Jeremiah 39:15–18}
{key: Bb}
{tempo: 71}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bb] | [F/A] | [Gm] | [Eb] | ×2

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Bb]Jeremiah waits in the guard court a[F/A]lone
The word of [Gm]the Lord breaks the heavy stone
[Eb]A message [Bb]is sent to E-bed-m-elech
[F/A]For the Cushite man who [Gm]holds his breath
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
The c[Eb]ity faces dis[Cm7]aster and not good
The words [Gm]will pass before his [Cm7]eyes in the flood
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
But I will [Fsus4]rescue you on that [F]day
You will [Bb]not be handed over [F]in fear
I will sure[Gm]ly deliver you a[Eb]way
You will [Bb]escape with your life, I [F]swear
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
The men you [Eb]dread will not [F]take you [Bb]down [F/A][Gm][Eb]
[Bb]Your trust in me has saved [F/A]the crown
You [Gm]have trusted in me, [Eb]declares the Lord
[Bb]A life preserved by the mighty [F/A]word
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
But [Gm]I will rescue you on [Eb]that day
You will not be hand[Bb]ed over in fear
[F]I will surely de[Gm]liver you away
[Eb]You will es[Bb]cape with your life, I [F]swear
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
The sword shall [Eb]not fall, the [F]doom is [Bb]gone
[Cm7]The promise stands [Gm]like the rising [F]sun
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Cm7]But I will res[Gm]cue you on that day
[F]You will not be handed [Bb]over in fear
I will [F]surely deliver [Gm7]you away
You will [Eb]escape with [Bb]your life, I [F]swear
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
Because you [Eb]have trusted [F]in [Bb]me
{end_of_verse}

